# Every platform a release publishes, and therefore every platform CI builds.
#
# ONE LIST, READ BY BOTH WORKFLOWS. release.yml builds these into archives and
# ci.yml cross-compiles them on every push. Two copies would drift, and the copy
# that drifts is the one guarding what people download — the same reasoning that
# makes release.yml call ci.yml rather than repeat its steps.
#
# Format: goos goarch [goarm]. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# Adding a platform is a line. Go cross-compiles to far more than this; shipping
# twenty archives nobody downloads is noise rather than generosity.
linux   amd64
linux   arm64
linux   arm   7
linux   386
darwin  amd64
darwin  arm64
windows amd64
windows arm64
